cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite the manuscript and the Zenodo deposit listed in the repository README."
title: "Transcriptomic Footprint of the Lysine-Pyruvylation Regulatory Network in Diabetic Foot Ulcer Tissue"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a public-data re-analysis of the lysine-pyruvylation
  (Kpy) regulatory network in diabetic foot ulcer tissue across 10 GEO cohorts,
  integrating differential-expression meta-analysis, weighted gene co-expression
  network analysis, a four-algorithm consensus machine-learning framework,
  immune deconvolution, single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, cis-eQTL Mendelian
  randomisation and molecular docking. The package contains all analysis code,
  derived result tables, figures, manuscript text and a machine-readable audit
  ledger tracing every numeric claim to its source file. Kpy modification itself
  was not measured; all findings concern the transcriptional footprint of the
  network.
